    path: 'vehicles/3145/NTNU/Balac Strike VTOL (Hybrid).blk',
    sha256: '9c7a046050a66e970d3a985074dd83c438ad886ae86d4c592bb9c930809fb2c0',
    content:
      "# MegaMek Data (C) 2025-2026 by The MegaMek Team is licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.\n# To view a copy of this license, visit https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\n#\n# NOTICE: The MegaMek organization is a non-profit group of volunteers\n# creating free software for the BattleTech community.\n#\n# MechWarrior, BattleMech, `Mech and AeroTech are registered trademarks\n# of The Topps Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved.\n#\n# Catalyst Game Labs and the Catalyst Game Labs logo are trademarks of\n# InMediaRes Productions, LLC.\n#\n# MechWarrior Copyright Microsoft Corporation. MegaMek Data was created under\n# Microsoft's \"Game Content Usage Rules\"\n# <https://www.xbox.com/en-US/developers/rules> and it is not endorsed by or\n# affiliated with Microsoft.\n\n#Saved from version 0.51.01 on 2026-07-12\n<UUID>\n019f583e-e824-7247-b16d-bfc39d7784e1\n</UUID>\n\n<UnitType>\nVTOL\n</UnitType>\n\n<Name>\nBalac Strike VTOL\n</Name>\n\n<Model>\n(Hybrid)\n</Model>\n\n<mul id:>\n6750\n</mul id:>\n\n<year>\n3090\n</year>\n\n<type>\nClan Level 3\n</type>\n\n<role>\nStriker\n</role>\n\n<quirks>\nvtol_rotor_coaxial\n</quirks>\n\n<motion_type>\nVTOL\n</motion_type>\n\n<cruiseMP>\n10\n</cruiseMP>\n\n<engine_type>\n0\n</engine_type>\n\n<clan_engine>\nfalse\n</clan_engine>\n\n<armor_type>\n1\n</armor_type>\n\n<armor_tech_rating>\n0\n</armor_tech_rating>\n\n<armor_tech_level>\n6\n</armor_tech_level>\n\n<armor>\n15\n12\n12\n7\n2\n</armor>\n\n<Body Equipment>\nClan Ammo ATM-6\nClan Ammo ATM-6\nCLCASE\nClan Heavy Machine Gun Ammo - Half\n</Body Equipment>\n\n<Front Equipment>\nCLATM6\nCLATM6\nCLHeavyMG\n</Front Equipment>\n\n<Right Equipment>\n</Right Equipment>\n\n<Left Equipment>\n</Left Equipment>\n\n<Rear Equipment>\n</Rear Equipment>\n\n<Rotor Equipment>\n</Rotor Equipment>\n\n<capabilities>\n<p>Configured for anti-vehicle fire support, the Balac centers its armament on a pair of Type 6 ATM-6 launchers capable of switching between standard, extended-range, and high-explosive ammunition to match tactical conditions. The launchers allow engagement well beyond the effective reach of most VTOL-mounted weapon systems, while a generous internal ammunition supply supports sustained operations without resupply. A Mk.3 ER medium laser serves as a secondary weapon for close-range threats and engagements that exhaust the ATM magazines.</p><p>The Consolidated 135 XL power plant provides a cruising speed of 119 kilometers per hour and a flank speed of 184, making the Balac exceptionally quick for its mass class. Forging AM15 ferro-fibrous armor provides adequate protection against glancing strikes from vehicle-grade weapons, though it is insufficient to absorb repeated direct hits from heavy systems. Most Balac crews exploit the craft's speed advantage by engaging from hover at range, firing over friendly-cleared terrain, or orbiting enemy formations at flank speed to present a difficult targeting solution while cycling through their ammunition load. One noted vulnerability is the risk of close-range surprise from advancing vehicles or BattleMechs on terrain not yet vetted by friendly forces.</p><p>The Neil 9000 Comm System and RCA Econotrac targeting suite support coordinated anti-vehicle operations across the ATM envelope, with the electronics package optimized for the Balac's vehicle-hunting design role.</p>\n</capabilities>\n\n<overview>\n<p>The Balac Strike VTOL is a post-Jihad design developed by Clan Diamond Shark in 3079 to capture the vehicle acquisition market anticipated in the conflict's aftermath. Expecting Inner Sphere and Clan forces to prioritize ground vehicle rebuilding over BattleMech procurement, the Sharks identified a gap in the VTOL fire support market and developed the Balac as a purpose-built platform from a clean design foundation independent of any existing Clan VTOL program. Despite incorporating Clan-grade technology, the Balac remains among the more cost-effective means of delivering extended-range anti-vehicle firepower to the field. The Sharks marketed it broadly to both Clan and Inner Sphere buyers, and the design's solid performance and manageable maintenance profile made it a commercial success before demilitarization trends across the Inner Sphere moderated demand.</p>\n</overview>\n\n<deployment>\n<p>The Hybrid configuration, introduced in 3090, blends Clan and Inner Sphere components to reduce production costs and expand the Balac's manufacturing accessibility beyond Diamond Shark-aligned facilities. Developed in part to serve markets where access to pure Clan-specification components was inconsistent, the configuration adjusts both armament and propulsion systems to reflect its mixed technology base. Field performance is broadly comparable to the base configuration in the anti-vehicle role, though Hybrid Balacs require coordination with maintenance personnel experienced in mixed-tech servicing. The design sees service primarily in regions where supply chain diversity is a practical operational advantage.</p>\n</deployment>\n\n<history>\n<p>The Balac entered service in 3079 as a deliberately commercial product rather than a military necessity. Clan Diamond Shark's analysts projected that both Inner Sphere governments and Clan toumans would need to rebuild substantial conventional vehicle forces after the Jihad, and the Sharks moved to position themselves as a primary supplier before reconstruction demand peaked. Rather than adapting an existing platform, they undertook a clean-sheet development effort independent of established Clan VTOL programs, with the explicit goal of producing a craft optimized for their anticipated customer requirements rather than Clan doctrine or legacy design constraints.</p><p>The decision to incorporate an XL fusion engine and top-grade ATM launchers ran counter to the cost-reduction impulse common in post-Jihad manufacturing, but the Sharks calculated that delivering genuine performance at a competitive price would drive volume sales more effectively than marginal cost savings. That calculation proved accurate through the early Dark Age period. The Balac found buyers across a broad spectrum, including frontline Clan units, Inner Sphere standing armies, and mercenary commands operating in the contested border zones left by the Jihad's upheavals.</p><p>Demand contracted significantly as Exarch Jonah Levin's rebuilding philosophy emphasized economic conversion over military expansion, reducing procurement budgets across much of the Inner Sphere. The Republic of the Sphere and aligned states curtailed vehicle acquisition, shifting the Balac's primary customer base toward mercenary commands and Periphery states with fewer ties to the Republic's demilitarization goals. By the 3130s, the design had largely transitioned to secondary market status, with newer Sea Fox designs filling frontline roles while Balacs continued service among forces with less frequent access to the latest procurement channels.</p>\n</history>\n\n<manufacturer>\nNew York Vehicle Y2 Facility\n</manufacturer>\n\n<primaryFactory>\nTrondheim\n</primaryFactory>\n\n<systemManufacturers>\nCHASSIS:Unknown\nENGINE:Unknown\nARMOR:Unknown\nJUMP_JET:N/A\nCOMMUNICATIONS:Unknown\nTARGETING:Unknown\n</systemManufacturers>\n\n<systemModels>\nCHASSIS:Unknown\nENGINE:Unknown\nARMOR:Unknown\nJUMP_JET:N/A\nCOMMUNICATIONS:Unknown\nTARGETING:Unknown\n</systemModels>\n\n<source>\nTR:3145\n</source>\n\n<published>\nRS:3145\n</published>\n\n<tonnage>\n25.0\n</tonnage>\n\n",
